    "For one observer under this park's sky; a rough guide.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For one observer under this park's sky; a rough guide."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Para un observador bajo el cielo de este parque; una guía aproximada."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For the next seven days, Nyx also asks three independent forecast models (NOAA's GFS, ECMWF's IFS and DWD's ICON) for the same dark window. When their averages are within 15 points of cloud cover they agree; within 35 they roughly agree; beyond that they disagree, and the time river draws the range of scores they allow. The score itself always uses Open-Meteo's best-match forecast. Cloud layers, the coldest hour, dew risk (air within 2 °C of its dew point) and the strongest gust come from the same seven-day forecast. Visibility is a coarse model value and appears only as a haze hint. None of these change the score.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For the next seven days, Nyx also asks three independent forecast models (NOAA's GFS, ECMWF's IFS and DWD's ICON) for the same dark window. When their averages are within 15 points of cloud cover they agree; within 35 they roughly agree; beyond that they disagree, and the time river draws the range of scores they allow. The score itself always uses Open-Meteo's best-match forecast. Cloud layers, the coldest hour, dew risk (air within 2 °C of its dew point) and the strongest gust come from the same seven-day forecast. Visibility is a coarse model value and appears only as a haze hint. None of these change the score."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Durante los próximos siete días, Nyx también consulta tres modelos de pronóstico independientes (GFS de NOAA, IFS de ECMWF e ICON de DWD) para el mismo periodo de oscuridad. Si sus promedios están a 15 puntos de nubosidad o menos, coinciden; a 35 o menos, coinciden aproximadamente; con más diferencia, discrepan, y el río del tiempo dibuja el rango de índices que permiten. El índice siempre usa el pronóstico de mejor ajuste de Open-Meteo. Las capas de nubes, la hora más fría, el riesgo de rocío (aire a menos de 2 °C de su punto de rocío) y la ráfaga más fuerte provienen del mismo pronóstico de siete días. La visibilidad es un valor aproximado del modelo y solo aparece como indicio de bruma. Nada de esto cambia el índice."
          }
        }
      }
    },
