      }
    },
    "Solar timing uses NOAA approximations. Moonrise and moonset use a low-precision Meeus-style position; allow about 15 minutes, and more near the poles or a blocked horizon. Moon illumination corrects the mean 29.53-day cycle with the Moon’s calculated position and is approximate. Terrain and atmospheric conditions can shift visible rise and set times. The Moon is drawn from NASA's lunar colour map (NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio, CGI Moon Kit), lit from the Sun's real direction and tilted as it appears from the park at its highest point that night.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Solar timing uses NOAA approximations. Moonrise and moonset use a low-precision Meeus-style position; allow about 15 minutes, and more near the poles or a blocked horizon. Moon illumination corrects the mean 29.53-day cycle with the Moon’s calculated position and is approximate. Terrain and atmospheric conditions can shift visible rise and set times. The Moon is drawn from NASA's lunar colour map (NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio, CGI Moon Kit), lit from the Sun's real direction and tilted as it appears from the park at its highest point that night."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Los horarios solares usan aproximaciones de NOAA. La salida y la puesta de la Luna usan una posición de baja precisión al estilo de Meeus; considera un margen de unos 15 minutos, y más cerca de los polos o con el horizonte obstruido. La iluminación lunar corrige el ciclo medio de 29.53 días con la posición calculada de la Luna y es aproximada. El terreno y las condiciones atmosféricas pueden alterar las horas visibles de salida y puesta. La Luna se dibuja con el mapa de color lunar de la NASA (Scientific Visualization Studio de la NASA, CGI Moon Kit), iluminada desde la dirección real del Sol e inclinada como se ve desde el parque en su punto más alto esa noche."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Solid: full forecast. Hollow: moon and darkness only. Dot size follows the score; a cloud marks overcast skies. A small streak marks a meteor shower's peak, a shaded Moon a lunar eclipse you can see; neither changes the score.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Solid: full forecast. Hollow: moon and darkness only. Dot size follows the score; a cloud marks overcast skies. A small streak marks a meteor shower's peak, a shaded Moon a lunar eclipse you can see; neither changes the score."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Relleno: pronóstico completo. Sin relleno: solo Luna y oscuridad. El tamaño del punto sigue al índice; una nube indica cielo cubierto. Un pequeño trazo marca el máximo de una lluvia de meteoros, y una Luna sombreada, un eclipse de Luna visible; ninguno cambia el índice."
          }
        }
      }
    },
