            "state": "translated",
            "value": "La Vía Láctea proyectaba una sombra tenue sobre el sendero."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Milky Way core is up at %@": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Milky Way core is up at %@"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "El núcleo de la Vía Láctea ya salió en %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Milky Way's bright center is Sagittarius A*, counted as up once it is 10° clear of the horizon. Planets use Paul Schlyter's low-precision orbital elements and agree with a professional ephemeris to within about a degree from 2026 to 2032; brightness is given in words, because Mercury's can be off by more than half a magnitude. Rise, set and best times are found to within a minute of the model, but hills, trees and haze can shift what you see by a few minutes or more. Meteor showers come from the International Meteor Organization's calendar (IMO, 2026 edition): dates, radiants and published peak rates. Nyx estimates an hourly rate for one observer from the radiant's height, the Moon and the park's estimated sky brightness; it is a rough guide, and real showers vary from year to year. Lunar eclipse times come from NASA's predictions by Fred Espenak (NASA/GSFC); Nyx checks the Moon's height at the park itself. None of this changes the score.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Milky Way's bright center is Sagittarius A*, counted as up once it is 10° clear of the horizon. Planets use Paul Schlyter's low-precision orbital elements and agree with a professional ephemeris to within about a degree from 2026 to 2032; brightness is given in words, because Mercury's can be off by more than half a magnitude. Rise, set and best times are found to within a minute of the model, but hills, trees and haze can shift what you see by a few minutes or more. Meteor showers come from the International Meteor Organization's calendar (IMO, 2026 edition): dates, radiants and published peak rates. Nyx estimates an hourly rate for one observer from the radiant's height, the Moon and the park's estimated sky brightness; it is a rough guide, and real showers vary from year to year. Lunar eclipse times come from NASA's predictions by Fred Espenak (NASA/GSFC); Nyx checks the Moon's height at the park itself. None of this changes the score."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "El centro brillante de la Vía Láctea es Sagitario A*, que se considera sobre el horizonte cuando supera los 10°. Los planetas usan los elementos orbitales de baja precisión de Paul Schlyter y coinciden con una efeméride profesional con un margen de un grado entre 2026 y 2032; el brillo se da con palabras, porque el de Mercurio puede desviarse más de media magnitud. Las horas de salida, puesta y mejor momento se calculan con un margen de un minuto respecto al modelo, pero las colinas, los árboles y la bruma pueden cambiar lo que ves en unos minutos o más. Las lluvias de meteoros provienen del calendario de la International Meteor Organization (IMO, edición 2026): fechas, radiantes y tasas máximas publicadas. Nyx estima una tasa por hora para un observador a partir de la altura del radiante, la Luna y el brillo estimado del cielo del parque; es una guía aproximada, y las lluvias reales varían de un año a otro. Los horarios de los eclipses de Luna provienen de las predicciones de la NASA de Fred Espenak (NASA/GSFC); Nyx comprueba la altura de la Luna en el propio parque. Nada de esto cambia el índice."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Milky Way's bright center stays at or below the horizon this far north. Its fainter band still crosses dark skies.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Milky Way's bright center stays at or below the horizon this far north. Its fainter band still crosses dark skies."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tan al norte, el centro brillante de la Vía Láctea se queda en el horizonte o por debajo. Su banda más tenue aún cruza los cielos oscuros."
          }
        }
      }
    },
